Drop the unused-function pragmas from lz4hc.c.

lz4hc.c includes lz4.c with LZ4_COMMONDEFS_ONLY to share its helpers, and
silences the resulting unused static functions with
`#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wunused-function"` and the clang
equivalent. R CMD check reports any `#pragma (GCC|clang) diagnostic
ignored` under src/ as a NOTE ("pragma(s) suppressing diagnostics"), and
CRAN's automated pretest archives a submission on a NOTE, so the pragmas
cannot ship.

Removing them changes no generated code. The only effect is that a build
with -Wall may print -Wunused-function warnings for lz4hc.c, which R CMD
check does not classify as significant.

--- a/lz4hc.c
+++ b/lz4hc.c
@@ -57,12 +57,6 @@
 
 /*===   Shared lz4.c code   ===*/
 #ifndef LZ4_SRC_INCLUDED
-# if defined(__GNUC__)
-#  pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wunused-function"
-# endif
-# if defined (__clang__)
-#  pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wunused-function"
-# endif
 # define LZ4_COMMONDEFS_ONLY
 # include "lz4.c"   /* LZ4_count, constants, mem */
 #endif
